    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d50">

                <pb facs="0108" n="34" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg34"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3997</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-21T17:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 21, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>928. Italy will send commission to United States probably headed by Duke of
                    Abruzzi. Some apprehension seems felt about threats of Socialists and clericals
                    to utilize May 1 for demonstrations against war. This partly explains absence of
                    public demonstration participated in by Government on our entry in war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
